{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1450425-military-equipment","id":1450425,"title":"Military Equipment","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-31T03:01:54-07:00","id":1450425,"title":"Military Equipment","content":"Is this something we should be expecting in the upcoming Hunter books? or has anyone started hardcore mundane firearms already?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5519-azerkatil","name":"Azerkatil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T03:15:35-07:00","id":1450429,"title":"","content":"WOD: Armory has a fairly extensive amount of coverage for military grade hardware (of all sorts, not just weapons). It would take a bit of converting to 2e, but it's there for people interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T03:18:21-07:00","id":1450430,"title":"","content":"I was really considering converting Armory my self, but if someone had something along the same lines, that would have been rad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5519-azerkatil","name":"Azerkatil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T06:46:50-07:00","id":1450682,"title":"","content":"There's a brief yet comprehensive few lines in Hurt Locker about how to convert the weaponry over from Armory. There's not much to it, weapons haven't changed that drastically across editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T10:23:33-07:00","id":1450694,"title":"","content":"The hardest part about converting stuff is weapons getting an initiative penalty, which is a purely meta-conceit and generally goes up as Damage goes up as a matter of combat balance rather than reflecting anything innately difficulty about handling those weapons. That said, it's not hard in a complex sense, but more in a time consuming judgement call sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}